---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Stackin Paper | ML Research Portfolio">
  <main class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6 py-12 font-sans text-slate-900">
    <header class="mb-8">
		<h1 class="text-3xl md:text-5xl font-serif italic tracking-tight text-[#bdaa8b]">
			Stackin Paper: Building on ML Research
		</h1>
	</header>
		
	<p class="text-xl leading-relaxed text-slate-700 mb-4">
		Welcome to <strong>Stackin Paper</strong>! This is my personal playground for breaking down the latest machine learning research papers, implementing them from scratch, and bridging the gap between intertwined topics; all while documenting my findings along the way.
	</p>


	<h3 class="text-xl md:text-3xl text-[#bdaa8b] tracking-tight mt-8 mb-2 font-serif underline">
		Objectives
	</h3>

  <p class="text-xl leading-relaxed text-slate-700 mb-4">
		I am particularly excited by, and aim to focus on, methodologies for enabling continual learning and long-horizon memory management. I believe them to be fundamental limitations preventing the progression of LLMs beyond the current paradigm, and I want to spend my time there.
	</p>

  <p class="text-xl leading-relaxed text-slate-700 mb-4">
    Much work is already underway towards these effects by the community, and I have been eager to contribute. My goal is to develop complete, end-to-end implementations that build on and refine the cutting edge research being published.
	</p>

  <p class="text-xl leading-relaxed text-slate-700 mb-4">
    I aim to be selective & thorough in my work; extensively documenting both my failures and successes as I believe a vast portion of the learning process lies within the act of overcoming failure. I’d rather build 3 things I believe in, than 10 things just for the sake of it.
  </p>

    <section class="mt-12 mb-16">
      <h2 class="text-xl md:text-3xl text-[#bdaa8b] tracking-tight mt-8 mb-4 font-serif underline">Research Logs</h2>
      <div class="overflow-x-auto">
        <table class="w-full text-left border-collapse border-4 border-[#8c7a5d]">
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th class="border-2 border-[#bdaa8b] px-4 py-2">Date</th>
              <th class="border-2 border-[#bdaa8b] px-4 py-2">Paper / Topic</th>
              <th class="border-2 border-[#bdaa8b] px-4 py-2">Action</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <td class="p-3 border border-2 border-[#bdaa8b] font-bold">Feb 2026</td>
              <td class="p-3 border border-2 border-[#bdaa8b] italic">Gradient Regularization w/ DR.GRPO</td>
              <td class="p-3 border border-2 border-[#bdaa8b] text-blue-600 font-semibold"><a href="https://github.com/daksh-dangi/stackin-code/tree/main/Gradient-Reg">View Project</a></td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="p-3 border border-2 border-[#bdaa8b] font-bold">March 2026</td>
              <td class="p-3 border border-2 border-[#bdaa8b] italic">Power Sampling</td>
              <td class="p-3 border border-2 border-[#bdaa8b] text-blue-600 font-semibold"><a href="https://github.com/daksh-dangi/stackin-code/tree/main/PowerSampling/">View Project</a></td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="text-slate-400">
              <td class="p-3 border border-2 border-[#bdaa8b] italic">Upcoming</td>
              <td class="p-3 border border-2 border-[#bdaa8b]">Writing Context into Memory via Gradient Descent</td>
              <td class="p-3 border border-2 border-[#bdaa8b] italic">Being Implemented</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="text-slate-400">
              <td class="p-3 border border-2 border-[#bdaa8b] italic">Upcoming</td>
              <td class="p-3 border border-2 border-[#bdaa8b]">Self-Distillation Fine-Tuning</td>
              <td class="p-3 border border-2 border-[#bdaa8b] italic">Being Implemented</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </section>

	<section>
      <h2 class="text-xl md:text-3xl text-[#bdaa8b] tracking-tight mt-8 mb-2 font-serif underline">AI Disclosure</h2>
      <p class="text-xl leading-relaxed text-slate-700 mb-4">
		I will try to be as transparent as possible regarding my usage of AI where relevant. While it can certainly be tempting to speed up progress and rely entirely on AI to implement these papers, my pursuit of imperfection leaves me seemingly orthogonal to this predisposition.
	  </p>
	  <p class="text-xl leading-relaxed text-slate-700 mb-4">
	  	How can I learn, make mistakes, and be perfectly imperfect without touching upon the work myself ? The extent of my AI usage is to review & refine my conceptual understanding at the start of the project, and verify key implementation details at the end. I will do my best to point out if/where it's been used for other reasons in the articles.
	  </p>
	  <p class="text-xl leading-relaxed text-slate-700">
		Well, that and also this entire website was coded using AI. I am not a frontend developer :)
	  </p>
    </section>

  <h3 class="text-xl md:text-3xl text-[#bdaa8b] tracking-tight mt-8 mb-2 font-serif underline">
		Motivation
	</h3>
  
  <p class="text-xl leading-relaxed text-slate-700">
		When tasked with explaining my motivation for this endeavor, I fall back to a quote from one of my favorite shows, Bleach, to offer some insight:
	</p>

	<section class="bg-cyan-50 border-l-4 border-blue-500 p-6 my-3 italic text-slate-700 rounded-xl">
		"I dislike perfection. If something is perfect, there is nothing above it. There is no room for imagination. No space for intelligence or ability. [...] Be more wonderful than anything that existed before you, but never perfect."
	</section>

	<p class="text-xl leading-relaxed text-slate-700">
    The quote itself focuses on one aspect of perfection, namely that it forecloses growth. However, my lived experiences extend this meaning to one more aligned with my view. That is, even the <i>pursuit</i> of perfection forecloses growth. Chasing after a flawless first attempt stranded me at the starting line for the longest time; changing this mentality was one of the most defining moments of my college career. 
	</p>

  <p class="text-xl leading-relaxed text-slate-700 mt-4">
		Accepting failure as a byproduct of trying, and more importantly, building upon those failures has become my true goal - not chasing the veneer of "perfection". This mindset change enabled me to complete my undergrad in 3 years and my MS in 1, and it is that very mindset that motivates me today to grow as a researcher.
	</p>
  </main>
</Layout>